# telegram-topics proxy configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` (in this plugin dir, or in ~/.claude/channels/telegram-topics/)
# and fill in. The real process environment always wins over a .env file.
# This is the CONTRACT: exactly these keys, nothing else. A `.env` key that is
# not one of these is a mistake (decide deliberately whether it belongs here).
# Never commit the filled-in `.env` (it is gitignored) - the token is a secret.

# The ONE bot token the proxy owns. Only the proxy may run getUpdates on it.
# BotFather -> /setprivacy -> Disable, so the bot sees every topic message.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# The forum supergroup id (looks like -1001234567890). Updates from any other
# chat are dropped: this is the access control. Enable Topics on the group.
TELEGRAM_GROUP_CHAT_ID=

# Working directory for every spawned topic-Claude. Optional; defaults to $HOME.
TELEGRAM_TOPICS_SPAWN_DIR=

# HTTP port the MCP clients long-poll / POST to. Optional; defaults to 8790.
TELEGRAM_PROXY_PORT=

# Channel marketplace ref passed to the launcher's
# --dangerously-load-development-channels. Optional; defaults to
# plugin:telegram@zamua. Change only if you renamed the marketplace.
TELEGRAM_TOPICS_MARKETPLACE=

# Nightly restart hour (0-23, LOCAL time). Optional; unset/empty = disabled.
# When set, once a day at this hour the proxy kills every LIVE topic session;
# each one re-spawns with --resume (fresh claude + latest launcher, full history
# kept) on its next inbound message. Passive: idle sessions are not kept running.
TELEGRAM_TOPICS_NIGHTLY_RESTART_HOUR=

# Run every topic-Claude at ultracode (xhigh) effort + standing-workflow
# orchestration. Optional; defaults to ON (true/1/yes/on; false/0/no/off = the
# default medium effort). The proxy bakes `"ultracode": <this>` into the
# generated effective-settings.json each start, so a change takes effect on the
# next proxy restart. (The single-session bridge sets ultracode in its own
# --settings override, independent of this.)
TELEGRAM_TOPICS_ULTRACODE=

# Default model for every topic-Claude (a model id, e.g. claude-fable-5 /
# claude-opus-4-8 / claude-sonnet-5, or an alias). Optional; defaults to
# claude-fable-5. Set `default` / `inherit` / empty to leave it unset (use the
# account default). Passed as the `--model` FLAG (not a settings key: a settings
# `model` is a default that a --resume'd session ignores; the flag overrides even
# on resume). Takes effect on each topic's next respawn. (The single-session
# bridge picks its own model separately.)
TELEGRAM_TOPICS_MODEL=

# Which terminal multiplexer hosts the detached topic-Claude sessions:
# `tmux` (default) or `herdr` (herdr.dev - per-agent state visibility, socket
# API, sessions survive client detach). Optional. Takes effect on the next
# proxy restart; sessions ALREADY running in the other multiplexer keep
# working (the proxy re-adopts what it finds in the registry) but can only be
# killed/respawned by the currently selected backend, so migrate live sessions
# deliberately: kill each session in the old backend and let its next inbound
# message respawn it (same claude session id -> same conversation) under the
# new one. herdr prerequisites (see CLAUDE.md "Multiplexer backends"): the
# herdr server must be running (e.g. a launchd agent running `herdr server`),
# and on macOS grant Full Disk Access to the herdr binary if your sessions
# need it (herdr becomes the TCC "responsible process", as tmux is today).
TELEGRAM_TOPICS_MULTIPLEXER=
